# HTML & CSS rules

## HTML pages

- One file per section at repo root; share nav, footer, and meta patterns with `index.html`
- Bootstrap 4.3 grid (`container`, `row`, `col-*`)
- CDN assets must include `integrity` and `crossorigin` where already used
- Nav links to `projects.html` are labelled **New Masjid** (not "Projects")
- Script tag for app JS (do not change filename manually):

```html
<script defer type="text/javascript" src="assets/js/scripts-{timestamp}.js"></script>
```

- Main stylesheet link (do not change filename manually):

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/css/main-{timestamp}.css">
```

## CSS

- `assets/css/main-{timestamp}.css` — layout, typography, components, motion, campaign page styles, responsive rules
- Extend Bootstrap; avoid overriding core Bootstrap class names unnecessarily
- Prefer existing colour/spacing variables and class names before adding new ones

### Campaign page (`projects.html`)

Use existing `campaign-*` namespace in `main.css`:

- Layout: `campaign-section`, `campaign-section-warm`, `campaign-section-title`
- Hero: `campaign-hero-panel`, `campaign-hero-unified`, `campaign-gfm-widget`, `bg-cover-projects`
- Cards: `campaign-reward-card`, `campaign-facility-card`, `campaign-cost-card`
- Buttons: `btn-campaign`, `btn-campaign-outline`
- Gallery: `grid-gallery` (BaguetteBox lightbox)

GoFundMe widgets use iframes with class `gfm-stream-goal-bar` or `gfm-embed` divs with `data-url`.

## Images

- Store under `assets/images/` in role-based subfolders:
  - `brand/` — logo, Bismillah text, decorative quotes
  - `backgrounds/` — CSS hero and section backgrounds
  - `photos/` — site and building photography
  - `blueprints/` — 3D renders, site plans, construction updates
  - `posters/`, `team/`, `ui/`
- Use descriptive `alt` text for accessibility
- Optimise file size before adding large images

## Text wrapping (headings & readable copy)

Never break words mid-character on small screens.

- **Do not use** Bootstrap `text-break` on headings, leads, or marketing copy — it sets aggressive `word-break` and causes orphan letters (e.g. `FOUNDATIO` / `N`).
- **Do use** the project utility class `text-wrap-safe` on hero titles, section headings, and paragraph blocks that must stay readable on mobile.
- Headings (`h1`–`h6`) already default to `overflow-wrap: normal` and `word-break: normal` in `main.css`.
- Prefer **responsive font size** (`clamp()`) over forced breaks when a title is too wide.
- Intentional line breaks: use `<br>` at word boundaries, or rephrase — not `text-break` / `word-break: break-all`.
- `word-break: break-all` is only for monospace codes, hashes, or URLs in dedicated UI (e.g. transaction codes) — never for prose or display headings.

```html
<!-- BAD -->
<h1 class="display-4 text-break">Give Your Child a Strong Islamic Foundation</h1>

<!-- GOOD -->
<h1 class="madrasa-hero-title text-wrap-safe">Give Your Child a Strong Islamic Foundation</h1>
```

## Accessibility

- Semantic headings (`h1` once per page; campaign hero may use `sr-only` h1 with visible blockquote)
- `lang="en-GB"` on `<html>`
- Sufficient colour contrast; don't rely on colour alone for meaning
- External links: `target="_blank"` with `rel="noopener"` where appropriate
